WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.383
Motherboards must provide physical slots and electrical PCI Express lanes suitable for the chosen GPUs.

00:00:07.383 --> 00:00:13.423
A full-length connector may operate with fewer lanes than its shape suggests.

00:00:13.423 --> 00:00:18.568
Consult platform documentation rather than assuming every slot is equivalent.

00:00:18.568 --> 00:00:22.371
Physical spacing is often the first constraint.

00:00:22.371 --> 00:00:27.069
Large coolers can block neighboring slots, cables, or airflow.

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:34.004
Chassis dimensions, card length, thickness, support brackets, and connector clearance must be checked together.

00:00:34.004 --> 00:00:42.729
Power-supply planning includes total capacity, transient demand, efficiency, connector type, cable limits, CPU and storage load, and margin.

00:00:42.729 --> 00:00:47.427
Do not improvise unsafe adapters or overload household circuits.

00:00:47.427 --> 00:00:50.335
Follow hardware-vendor and electrical guidance.

00:00:50.335 --> 00:00:57.718
Cooling must remove sustained heat from every card, the CPU, memory, storage, and power components.

00:00:57.718 --> 00:01:01.968
One GPU can feed hot exhaust into another.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:08.009
Airflow path, fan behavior, ambient temperature, dust filters, and noise targets matter.

00:01:08.009 --> 00:01:17.628
Risers and external-GPU arrangements can solve spacing or experimentation needs but add bandwidth, enclosure, cable, power, compatibility, and support considerations.

00:01:17.628 --> 00:01:22.774
They should be treated as distinct architectures, not invisible extensions.

00:01:22.774 --> 00:01:28.814
Mixed GPUs complicate memory balance, speed, features, driver support, precision, and scheduling.

00:01:28.814 --> 00:01:37.091
Workstation platforms may offer more lanes, spacing, memory, and management than consumer systems, but they add cost.

00:01:37.091 --> 00:01:40.000
Choose around the measured workload.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.040
Platform topology includes how slots connect to the CPU, chipset, and memory.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:51.633
Shared links or indirect paths can affect transfer and peer communication.

00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:56.331
Read the motherboard and processor lane diagrams before purchase.
